<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12876" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-κναίω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-κνάω</span></b> , inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κνᾶν</span> dub. l. <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Phlb.</u>
			26b
		</span></i>: aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έκναισα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					406b
				</span></i>
			:— <i>scrape, rub off,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				245
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινά</span>
			<i>wear</i> one <i>out, worry to death,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1087
			</span></i>, Pl.ll.cc., f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				7.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύ μ᾽ ἀποκναίεις περιπατῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					341
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκναίει γὰρ ἀηδίᾳ δήπου καὶ
					ἀναισθησίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.153
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				20
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be worn out,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				406b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσφοραῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					6.2.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
